# An enabled drop-in is local operator config, not source: it is how a given
# install chooses to expose Neo4j, and it may grow site-specific gating. Only
# the *.conf.example templates, and the one drop-in named at the end, belong
# in git.
#
# `*.conf` does not match `neo4j.conf.example`, so the templates stay tracked.
*.conf

# The one tracked drop-in: the page shown instead of a bare 502 while the app
# restarts. It is always on, so it belongs in git.
!error-pages.conf
